   "design": "The planning system ({OPS_SYSTEM}) lists due jobs from contract frequencies and client requests, shows crew leave and machine bookings, and flags jobs the forecast rules out (no spraying in wind, no mowing in heavy rain). Fixed rules propose a week schedule by skills, equipment and travel distance, never by individual speed or behaviour; the supervisor adjusts it, and only then is it pushed to crew phones. Rescheduling after rain or breakdowns stays with the supervisor.",
   "previous_blocker": "Due work, availability and weather were pieced together in spreadsheets and calls.",
   "enabler_now": "Planning tools hold contract frequencies, availability and rules, and push schedules to phones.",
   "still_hard": "Dutch weather changes plans daily; the supervisor still juggles.",
   "human_edge": "Knowing which client will accept a delay and which will not.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "none",
    "what": ""
   },
   "altitude": "The supervisor adjusts a proposed schedule instead of building it.",
   "reach": [
    {
     "role": "crew leader",
     "task": "Plan the crew's day",
     "learn": "Whether phone schedules cut morning calls."
    }
   ],
